The GRIDE likelihood solver and the TwoNN fitting procedure in
src/req_metrics/metrics/dimension.py are ports of DADApy's
_utils/utils.py (_filter_mus, _neg_dloglik_did, _argmax_loglik,
_fisher_info_scaling) and id_estimation.py (_compute_id_2NN,
return_id_scaling_gride). Changes: rewritten on torch tensors, neighbor
distances taken from a shared precomputed table instead of recomputed per
call, scales exposed by their outer neighbor rank, results returned as
MetricResult. Numerical parity with DADApy is checked in tests/test_dadapy_parity.py.

Method references for every metric are listed in docs/references.bib; the
toolkit asks users to cite the original paper of each metric they report.

The bias-corrected participation-ratio formulas in req_metrics/metrics/spectral.py
(participation_ratio with correction="row" or "both") follow the estimators of
Chun, Canatar, Chung and Lee (ICLR 2026) and their reference implementation
https://github.com/badooki/dimensionality (MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Chan Woo
Chun). The quartic index sums are computed here in closed form from the Gram matrix
and column moments and are checked against that implementation.
